  "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Megabonk Mods Guide: Install, Best Mods & Safety</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Install Megabonk mods with r2modman or Gale. Compare Thunderstore mods, check compatibility, back up saves, uninstall safely, and fix broken profiles.\">\n    <meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"megabonk mods, megabonk mod, how to mod megabonk, megabonk modding, megabonk nexus, thunderstore megabonk\">\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-image-preview:large\">\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://megabonk.org/mods/\">\n\n    <script async src=\"https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-8830315294299920\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n    <script async src=\"https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-V5X87M8JFL\"></script>\n    <script>\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\n        function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }\n        gtag('js', new Date());\n        gtag('config', 'G-V5X87M8JFL');\n    </script>\n\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\">\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://megabonk.org/mods/\">\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Megabonk.org\">\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Megabonk Mods Guide: Install, Compatibility & Safety\">\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Choose a mod manager, compare current mods, protect your save, and recover a clean Megabonk profile.\">\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://megabonk.org/images/megabonk.jpg\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Megabonk Mods & Modding Guide\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"Thunderstore setup, popular mods, compatibility checks, backups, uninstall steps, and safety boundaries.\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://megabonk.org/images/megabonk.jpg\">\n\n    <script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n    {\n      \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n      \"@graph\": [\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"Article\",\n          \"headline\": \"Megabonk Mods Guide: Install, Best Mods and Safety\",\n          \"description\": \"A current guide to the unofficial Megabonk mod ecosystem, mod managers, BepInEx, compatibility, save backups, uninstalling, and troubleshooting.\",\n          \"datePublished\": \"2026-07-24\",\n          \"dateModified\": \"2026-07-27\",\n          \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Megabonk.org\"},\n          \"publisher\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Megabonk.org\"},\n          \"image\": \"https://megabonk.org/images/megabonk.jpg\",\n          \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\"@id\": \"https://megabonk.org/mods/#webpage\"}\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\n          \"@id\": \"https://megabonk.org/mods/#webpage\",\n          \"url\": \"https://megabonk.org/mods/\",\n          \"name\": \"Megabonk Mods Guide\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"HowTo\",\n          \"name\": \"How to install Megabonk mods with a mod manager\",\n          \"step\": [\n            {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"name\": \"Back up the save\", \"text\": \"Close Megabonk and copy the complete save folder before installing a loader or gameplay mod.\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"name\": \"Install a trusted manager\", \"text\": \"Install r2modman or Gale from its original Thunderstore or GitHub page.\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"name\": \"Create a Megabonk profile\", \"text\": \"Select Megabonk and create a separate profile instead of changing the clean setup.\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"name\": \"Install one mod\", \"text\": \"Install one current package and allow the manager to install its declared BepInEx dependencies.\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"name\": \"Launch modded\", \"text\": \"Start the game through the manager's modded launch option and test the title screen and one short run.\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"HowToStep\", \"name\": \"Add mods gradually\", \"text\": \"Add one mod at a time so a broken dependency or conflict is easy to identify.\"}\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"ItemList\",\n          \"name\": \"Popular Megabonk mods and tools\",\n          \"itemListElement\": [\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"r2modman\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Gale Mod Manager\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"MegabonkTogether\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 4, \"name\": \"BonkWithFriends\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 5, \"name\": \"CustomCharacterCreator\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 6, \"name\": \"SpawnTracker\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 7, \"name\": \"UsefullInfoUI\", \"url\": \"https://megabonk.org/mods/usefulinfoui/\"}\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n          \"mainEntity\": [\n            {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Does Megabonk officially support mods?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Megabonk does not list a built-in mod browser or Steam Workshop support. The available mod ecosystem is community-made and commonly distributed through Thunderstore.\"}},\n            {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"What is the easiest way to install Megabonk mods?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Use a Thunderstore-compatible manager such as r2modman or Gale, create a separate Megabonk profile, and let the manager install each package's declared BepInEx dependencies.\"}},\n            {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Are Megabonk mods safe?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"No third-party code is risk-free. Prefer original Thunderstore and linked source pages, check authors and update dates, back up saves, avoid unknown installers, and keep gameplay-changing mods away from official leaderboard submissions.\"}},\n            {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Where are Megabonk mods downloaded?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Thunderstore is the main organized Megabonk catalog. Use original package pages and author-linked GitHub repositories rather than search-result reuploads.\"}},\n            {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"How do I uninstall all Megabonk mods?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Disable the modded profile or create a clean profile in the manager. If the vanilla game still fails, verify the game files in Steam and restore a known-good save only when needed.\"}},\n            {\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Do Megabonk mods work after every update?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Not automatically. A game update can break the loader, dependencies, or individual mods. Compare the game version, package update date, changelog, dependencies, and recent reports before launching an important save.\"}}\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\",\n          \"itemListElement\": [\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://megabonk.org/\"},\n            {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Mods\", \"item\": \"https://megabonk.org/mods/\"}\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n    </script>\n\n    <style>\n        :root {\n            --bg: #101114;\n            --surface: #1b1e23;\n            --surface-2: #24282f;\n            --border: #353a43;\n            --text: #f4f5f7;\n            --muted: #b0b6c0;\n            --orange: #ff7a35;\n            --cyan: #4dc5d6;\n            --green: #45c97a;\n            --yellow: #f4c95d;\n            --red: #ef6262;\n        }\n        * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n        html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }\n        body {\n            margin: 0;\n            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;\n            color: var(--text);\n            line-height: 1.65;\n            background: var(--bg);\n            overflow-x: hidden;\n        }\n        a { color: var(--cyan); }\n        .site-header {\n            position: sticky;\n            top: 0;\n            z-index: 100;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n            background: rgba(16,17,20,.95);\n            backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n        }\n        .nav-inner {\n            width: min(100% - 2rem, 1160px);\n            min-height: 66px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            gap: 1rem;\n        }\n        .logo { color: var(--orange); text-decoration: none; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 900; }\n        .nav-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-end; gap: .25rem; margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }\n        .nav-links a { display: block; padding: .45rem .65rem; color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 700; }\n        .nav-links a:hover, .nav-links a:focus-visible { color: var(--orange); }\n        .container { width: min(100% - 2rem, 1060px); margin: 0 auto; }\n        .breadcrumb { padding: 1.25rem 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .94rem; }\n        .breadcrumb a { text-decoration: none; }\n        .hero {\n            min-height: 430px;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: flex-end;\n            margin-bottom: 2rem;\n            border: 1px solid var(--border);\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(12,13,16,.97) 0%, rgba(12,13,16,.84) 52%, rgba(12,13,16,.30) 100%), url('/images/megabonk.jpg');\n            background-size: cover;\n            background-position: center;\n        }\n        .hero-content { max-width: 730px; padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); }\n        .eyebrow { color: var(--cyan); font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em; }\n        h1 { margin: .55rem 0 1rem; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.06; }\n        .hero p { margin: 0; color: #d4d8de; font-size: 1.12rem; }\n        .status-line { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; }\n        .status-line span { padding: .4rem .65rem; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18); border-radius: 6px; background: rgba(0,0,0,.45); font-size: .88rem; }\n        .quick-answer { margin: 0 0 2rem; padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem; border-left: 5px solid var(--orange); background: var(--surface); }\n        .quick-answer h2 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; padding: 0; border: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: 1.3rem; }\n        .quick-answer p { margin: 0; }\n        .toc { padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--surface); }\n        .toc strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .65rem; }\n        .toc-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; }\n        .toc a { padding: .42rem .7rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 650; }\n        .toc a:hover { border-color: var(--cyan); color: var(--cyan); }\n        section[id] { scroll-margin-top: 5.5rem; }\n        h2 { margin: 3.5rem 0 1.25rem; padding-bottom: .55rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border); font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 4vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.2; }\n        h3 { margin: 1.4rem 0 .55rem; font-size: 1.22rem; }\n        p { margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }\n        ul, ol { padding-left: 1.4rem; }\n        li { margin-bottom: .55rem; }\n        strong { color: #fff; }\n        .status-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--border); }\n        .status-item { min-width: 0; padding: 1.15rem; background: var(--surface); }\n        .status-item span { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .07em; }\n        .status-item strong { display: block; margin-top: .35rem; font-size: 1.02rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }\n        .decision-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; }\n        .decision { padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--surface); }\n        .decision .type { color: var(--cyan); font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; }\n        .decision h3 { margin: .3rem 0 .55rem; }\n        .decision p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }\n        .steps { counter-reset: install; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; }\n        .step { position: relative; min-height: 145px; padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.25rem 4rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface); }\n        .step::before { counter-increment: install; content: counter(install); position: absolute; top: 1.3rem; left: 1.25rem; display: grid; place-items: center; width: 2rem; height: 2rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--orange); color: #111; font-weight: 900; }\n        .step h3 { margin: 0 0 .45rem; }\n        .step p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }\n        .table-wrap { margin: 1rem 0 1.75rem; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; }\n        table { width: 100%; min-width: 840px; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--surface); }\n        th, td { padding: .85rem .9rem; border-right: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }\n        th { color: var(--cyan); background: #15171b; }\n        td { color: var(--muted); }\n        tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }\n        th:last-child, td:last-child { border-right: 0; }\n        .tag { display: inline-block; padding: .18rem .45rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 850; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .tag-tool { color: #101114; background: var(--cyan); }\n        .tag-low { color: #101114; background: var(--green); }\n        .tag-medium { color: #101114; background: var(--yellow); }\n        .tag-high { color: #fff; background: var(--red); }\n        .notice { margin: 1.25rem 0; padding: 1.2rem 1.35rem; border-left: 5px solid var(--yellow); background: var(--surface); }\n        .notice.danger { border-color: var(--red); }\n        .notice.good { border-color: var(--green); }\n        .notice p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); }\n        .checklist { padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem; border: 1px solid rgba(69,201,122,.45); background: rgba(69,201,122,.07); }\n        .checklist li::marker { color: var(--green); }\n        .flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; }\n        .flow-item { padding: 1.1rem; border-top: 4px solid var(--cyan); background: var(--surface); }\n        .flow-item strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .4rem; }\n        .flow-item p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .95rem; }\n        .source-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: .92rem; }\n        .source-note a { font-weight: 700; }\n        .faq details { margin-bottom: .75rem; padding: 1rem 1.15rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--surface); }\n        .faq summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 800; }\n        .faq p { margin: .75rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); }\n        .related { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; }\n        .related a { padding: 1.15rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; background: var(--surface); }\n        .related a:hover { border-color: var(--orange); }\n        .related span { display: block; color: var(--orange); font-weight: 850; }\n        footer { margin-top: 4rem; padding: 2.5rem 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); text-align: center; background: #15171b; }\n        @media (max-width: 820px) {\n            .status-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); }\n            .decision-grid, .related { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n            .flow { grid-template-columns: repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); }\n        }\n        @media (max-width: 620px) {\n            .nav-inner { width: min(100% - 1rem,1160px); align-items: flex-start; padding: .65rem 0; }\n            .nav-links a { padding: .35rem .4rem; font-size: .82rem; }\n            .container { width: min(100% - 1.25rem,1060px); }\n            .hero { min-height: 500px; background-position: 62% center; }\n            .hero-content { padding: 2rem 1.35rem; }\n            .steps, .flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n            .step { min-height: 0; }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header class=\"site-header\">\n        <nav class=\"nav-inner\" aria-label=\"Primary navigation\">\n            <a class=\"logo\" href=\"/\">Megabonk</a>\n            <ul class=\"nav-links\">\n                <li><a href=\"/guides/\">Guides</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"/guides/patch-notes/\">Patches</a></li>\n                <li><a href=\"/guides/save-recovery\">Save Help</a></li>\n            </ul>\n        </nav>\n    </header>\n\n    <main class=\"container\">\n        <nav class=\"breadcrumb\" aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a> &rsaquo; Mods</nav>\n\n        <section class=\"hero\">\n            <div class=\"hero-content\">\n                <span class=\"eyebrow\">Unofficial community tools</span>\n                <h1>Megabonk Mods & Modding Guide</h1>\n                <p>Choose the right manager, install a clean profile, compare active mods, check game-version compatibility, and recover safely when a package breaks.</p>\n                <div class=\"status-line\">\n                    <span>Game reference: v1.0.69</span>\n                    <span>Catalog checked: July 24, 2026</span>\n                    <span>129 Thunderstore packages</span>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"quick-answer\" aria-labelledby=\"quick-title\">\n            <h2 id=\"quick-title\">Does Megabonk support mods?</h2>\n            <p><strong>Community mods are available, but they are not an official built-in feature.</strong> Megabonk's Steam listing does not advertise a mod browser or Workshop integration. The organized community catalog is on <a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Thunderstore</a>; the easiest setup is a separate profile in r2modman or Gale, with BepInEx IL2CPP installed as a declared dependency.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Mods guide contents\">\n            <strong>On this page</strong>\n            <div class=\"toc-links\">\n                <a href=\"#status\">Current status</a>\n                <a href=\"#install\">Install</a>\n                <a href=\"#popular\">Popular mods</a>\n                <a href=\"#compatibility\">Compatibility</a>\n                <a href=\"#backup\">Backups</a>\n                <a href=\"#uninstall\">Uninstall</a>\n                <a href=\"#safety\">Safety</a>\n                <a href=\"#faq\">FAQ</a>\n            </div>\n        </nav>\n\n        <section id=\"status\">\n            <h2>Current Megabonk Modding Status</h2>\n            <div class=\"status-grid\">\n                <div class=\"status-item\"><span>Official support</span><strong>No built-in mod browser</strong></div>\n                <div class=\"status-item\"><span>Main catalog</span><strong>Thunderstore</strong></div>\n                <div class=\"status-item\"><span>Common loader</span><strong>BepInEx IL2CPP</strong></div>\n                <div class=\"status-item\"><span>Recommended setup</span><strong>Separate manager profile</strong></div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"source-note\">The Steam feature list includes single-player, achievements, cloud saves, stats, and leaderboards, but does not list Workshop support. Thunderstore showed 129 Megabonk packages when checked on July 24, 2026.</p>\n\n            <h3>Manager, loader, or mod?</h3>\n            <div class=\"decision-grid\">\n                <article class=\"decision\"><span class=\"type\">Manager</span><h3>r2modman or Gale</h3><p>Creates profiles, downloads packages, resolves declared dependencies, toggles mods, and launches a modded or vanilla session.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"decision\"><span class=\"type\">Loader</span><h3>BepInEx IL2CPP</h3><p>Loads compatible code into this Unity IL2CPP game. Most BepInEx mods declare the required pack version automatically.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"decision\"><span class=\"type\">Content</span><h3>Individual mods</h3><p>Add UI, characters, co-op, automation, or gameplay changes. Each package has its own dependencies and patch risk.</p></article>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"notice\"><p><strong>Searching for “Megabonk Nexus”?</strong> Use the original Thunderstore package or the author-linked GitHub repository when available. We did not find an official Nexus destination linked by the Steam listing or the selected package authors, so avoid treating a search-result reupload as authoritative.</p></div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"install\">\n            <h2>How to Install Megabonk Mods</h2>\n            <p>This manager-first route keeps mod files in a named profile and makes rollback much easier than copying random files into the game directory.</p>\n            <div class=\"steps\">\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Close the game and back up</h3><p>Exit Megabonk completely. Copy the whole save folder to a dated backup before changing the loader, profile, or save-affecting mods.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Install one manager</h3><p>Get <a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/ebkr/r2modman/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">r2modman</a> or <a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/Kesomannen/GaleModManager/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Gale</a> from its original page. Do not run an installer from a repost.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Select Megabonk</h3><p>Create a new profile named for the game version or purpose, such as “1.0.69 UI test.” Keep a clean profile for comparison.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Install one package</h3><p>Choose the Mod Manager install option. Accept the package's declared dependencies instead of downloading a random BepInEx build manually.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Launch modded</h3><p>Start through the manager's modded launch button. Confirm the title screen loads, then run a short low-stakes test before opening an important save.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Add mods one at a time</h3><p>After each successful test, add the next package. This makes a bad version, missing dependency, or conflict easy to isolate.</p></article>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"notice good\"><p><strong>Best baseline:</strong> one clean profile, one test profile, and one dated save backup. A profile name should record the game version and purpose rather than “new profile.”</p></div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"popular\">\n            <h2>Popular Megabonk Mods and Tools</h2>\n            <p>These are current Thunderstore package records, not a guarantee that every package works with every Megabonk patch or with every other mod.</p><div class=\"notice\"><p><strong>Looking specifically for co-op?</strong> Use the <a href=\"/mods/multiplayer/\">Megabonk Multiplayer Mod Guide</a> to compare MegabonkTogether and BonkWithFriends, match host/client profiles, back up saves, and troubleshoot desync.</p></div>\n            <div class=\"table-wrap\">\n                <table>\n                    <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Type</th><th>Listed version</th><th>Last package update</th><th>What it does</th><th>Risk</th></tr></thead>\n                    <tbody>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/ebkr/r2modman/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>r2modman</strong></a></td><td>Manager</td><td>3.2.18</td><td>Jun 25, 2026</td><td>Manages Thunderstore profiles, packages, dependencies, and launches.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-tool\">Tool</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/Kesomannen/GaleModManager/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Gale Mod Manager</strong></a></td><td>Manager</td><td>1.19.0</td><td>Jul 20, 2026</td><td>Lightweight Thunderstore-compatible manager and r2modman alternative.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-tool\">Tool</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/DShad/MegabonkTogether/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>MegabonkTogether</strong></a></td><td>Netplay</td><td>5.1.0</td><td>Jul 13, 2026</td><td>Adds community netplay. Every participant should use the same tested profile.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-high\">High</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/BonkWithFriends/BonkWithFriends/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>BonkWithFriends</strong></a></td><td>P2P co-op</td><td>0.4.1</td><td>Jul 8, 2026</td><td>Adds unofficial Steamworks P2P multiplayer and synchronization.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-high\">High</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/MegabonkModders/CustomCharacterCreator/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>CustomCharacterCreator</strong></a></td><td>Custom content</td><td>1.4.0</td><td>Oct 23, 2025</td><td>Loads custom characters and their associated content.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-medium\">Medium</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/Antiparty/SpawnTracker/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>SpawnTracker</strong></a></td><td>Overlay</td><td>0.5.6</td><td>Oct 21, 2025</td><td>Shows spawned and unopened chests, shrines, and ShadyGuys.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-medium\">Medium</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/wafuruns/MegabonkBetterMinimap/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>MegabonkBetterMinimap</strong></a></td><td>UI</td><td>1.4.1</td><td>Oct 9, 2025</td><td>Changes minimap sizing and zoom and adds full-map controls.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-medium\">Medium</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"https://thunderstore.io/c/megabonk/p/Helix128/StatHUD/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>StatHUD</strong></a></td><td>Overlay</td><td>1.2.1</td><td>Nov 1, 2025</td><td>Displays real-time DPS and additional run statistics.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-medium\">Medium</span></td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><a href=\"/mods/usefulinfoui/\"><strong>UsefullInfoUI</strong></a></td><td>UI overlay</td><td>1.2.0</td><td>Nov 5, 2025</td><td>Shows configurable run counts and player stats; package-tested on game v1.0.19.</td><td><span class=\"tag tag-medium\">Medium</span></td></tr>\n                    </tbody>\n                </table>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"source-note\">Versions and update dates are from Thunderstore's public Megabonk package data checked July 24, 2026. “Risk” reflects the breadth of game-state changes, not a malware verdict.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"compatibility\">\n            <h2>How to Check Mod Compatibility</h2>\n            <p>A recent package date is useful, but it is not proof. Check the whole chain before launching: game build, manager, loader, dependencies, mod, and other enabled packages.</p>\n            <div class=\"flow\">\n                <article class=\"flow-item\"><strong>1. Game version</strong><p>Record the current Megabonk version before updating or troubleshooting.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"flow-item\"><strong>2. Package record</strong><p>Read the package version, update date, changelog, and pinned instructions.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"flow-item\"><strong>3. Dependencies</strong><p>Check the exact BepInEx or library versions declared by that package.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"flow-item\"><strong>4. Recent reports</strong><p>Look for current issues mentioning your game and package versions.</p></article>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"table-wrap\">\n                <table>\n                    <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Signals</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead>\n                    <tbody>\n                        <tr><td><span class=\"tag tag-low\">Ready to test</span></td><td>Recent update or explicit current-version note; dependencies resolve; no current blocking issue.</td><td>Test it alone in a separate profile and disposable run.</td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><span class=\"tag tag-medium\">Unclear</span></td><td>Older package, no game-version claim, or mixed recent reports.</td><td>Keep it disabled on the main profile; wait or test only after a full backup.</td></tr>\n                        <tr><td><span class=\"tag tag-high\">Do not use yet</span></td><td>Deprecated package, unresolved loader error, missing dependency, crash loop, or save corruption report.</td><td>Remove it from the profile and use the last known-good version only if the author documents that rollback.</td></tr>\n                    </tbody>\n                </table>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"notice\"><p><strong>After a Megabonk update:</strong> launch vanilla first. Do not update the game, loader, and every mod simultaneously and then try to diagnose the result.</p></div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"backup\">\n            <h2>Back Up Your Save Before Modding</h2>\n            <ol class=\"checklist\">\n                <li>Exit Megabonk and the mod manager completely.</li>\n                <li>Open <code>%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\LocalLow\\</code> and locate the active Megabonk save directory. The final developer and save-folder names can vary, so confirm the folder from its recent files before copying it.</li>\n                <li>Copy the entire <code>Saves</code> folder to a separate dated folder.</li>\n                <li>Keep at least one backup made before installing any save editor, unlocker, item spawner, or multiplayer mod.</li>\n                <li>Do not edit the only copy of a save in place.</li>\n            </ol>\n            <p>Steam Cloud is useful, but synchronization is not the same as a versioned manual backup. If a modified or corrupted save syncs, the cloud copy may also become the wrong copy. See the <a href=\"/guides/save-recovery\">Megabonk Save Recovery Guide</a> before restoring files.</p>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"uninstall\">\n            <h2>How to Disable or Uninstall Mods</h2>\n            <div class=\"steps\">\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Disable the last mod</h3><p>Turn off the most recently added package, keep its required libraries in place, and test the profile again.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Disable all mods</h3><p>If the problem remains, disable the complete profile or switch to the clean profile. This separates game problems from mod problems.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Verify Steam files</h3><p>If vanilla still fails, use Steam's installed-files verification. This restores missing or changed game files without asking you to delete saves.</p></article>\n                <article class=\"step\"><h3>Restore only when needed</h3><p>Restore a dated save only if the problem follows the save into a verified clean game. Preserve the current copy before overwriting it.</p></article>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"notice danger\"><p><strong>Do not troubleshoot by deleting folders at random.</strong> A manager profile, the game installation, and the save folder are different layers. Identify which layer is broken before removing anything.</p></div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section id=\"safety\">\n            <h2>Mod Safety and Fair-Play Boundaries</h2>\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Third-party code can access your user account's files and network.</strong> Use original package pages, inspect linked source repositories when available, and avoid unknown executables or password-protected archives.</li>\n                <li><strong>Do not submit gameplay-changing modded runs to official leaderboards.</strong> Unlockers, item spawners, stat changes, automation, custom characters, and netplay make results incomparable with vanilla runs.</li>\n                <li><strong>Use matching multiplayer profiles.</strong> Different mod or dependency versions can cause desync, missing objects, or failed connections.</li>\n                <li><strong>Keep private data out of support logs.</strong> Review logs before posting them publicly and remove usernames, local paths, tokens, or invite details when present.</li>\n                <li><strong>Do not assume “popular” means harmless.</strong> Download count measures adoption, not security review or compatibility with your current setup.</li>\n            </ul>\n            <div class=\"notice danger\"><p><strong>Stop immediately</strong> if a package asks you to disable antivirus globally, enter a Steam password outside Steam, run an unrelated administrator script, or download dependencies from an unlisted mirror.</p></div>\n        </section>\n\n        <section class=\"faq\" id=\"faq\">\n            <h2>Megabonk Mods FAQ</h2>\n            <details><summary>Is the Megabonk Toggler a mod?</summary><p>No. Toggler is a native Shop Upgrade unlocked after purchasing 40 unlocks. It needs no download, manager, shortcut, or config file. Use the <a href=\"/guides/unlocks/toggler/\">Toggler unlock and usage guide</a>.</p></details>\n            <details><summary>Does Megabonk officially support mods?</summary><p>No built-in mod browser or Steam Workshop feature is listed for the game. Current mods are community projects and are used at your own risk.</p></details>\n            <details><summary>What is the easiest way to mod Megabonk?</summary><p>Install r2modman or Gale from its original page, select Megabonk, create a separate profile, and install one package through the manager so declared BepInEx dependencies are included.</p></details>\n            <details><summary>Should I use Nexus or Thunderstore for Megabonk mods?</summary><p>Thunderstore is the organized catalog used by the current Megabonk packages in this guide. Prefer original package pages and author-linked source repositories rather than an unverified reupload found through search.</p></details>\n            <details><summary>Are Megabonk mods safe?</summary><p>No third-party code is guaranteed safe. Back up saves, check the author and package history, use original sources, scan downloads, and avoid unknown installers. Keep gameplay-changing mods away from official leaderboard runs.</p></details>\n            <details><summary>Can mods add multiplayer?</summary><p>Yes. Community projects such as MegabonkTogether and BonkWithFriends add unofficial co-op. Compare their current versions, installation and risks in the <a href=\"/mods/multiplayer/\">Multiplayer Mod Guide</a>.</p></details>\n            <details><summary>Why did my mods stop working after an update?</summary><p>The update may have changed the game code expected by BepInEx, a library, or the mod itself. Launch vanilla, compare package and dependency versions, then re-enable one current mod at a time.</p></details>\n            <details><summary>How do I return to vanilla Megabonk?</summary><p>Switch to a clean manager profile or disable the modded profile. If vanilla still fails, verify installed files in Steam. Restore a save backup only if the clean verified game still has a save-specific problem.</p></details>\n        </section>\n\n        <section>\n            <h2>Related Guides</h2>\n            <div class=\"related\">\n                <a href=\"/guides/unlocks/toggler/\"><span>Toggler guide</span>The native pool-control upgrade, not a community mod</a>\n                <a href=\"/mods/multiplayer/\"><span>Multiplayer mods</span>Compare community co-op packages, setup, compatibility, and risks</a>\n                <a href=\"/mods/usefulinfoui/\"><span>UsefullInfoUI</span>Install, configure, troubleshoot, and cleanly remove the run overlay</a>\n                <a href=\"/faq/megabonk-cheats-trainers/\"><span>Cheats and trainers</span>Understand WeMod, cheat-table, save, security, and leaderboard risks</a>\n                <a href=\"/faq/is-megabonk-multiplayer\"><span>Official multiplayer status</span>Native co-op, Remote Play, and the current vanilla answer</a>\n                <a href=\"/guides/save-recovery\"><span>Protect progress</span>Back up, recover, and restore Megabonk saves</a>\n                <a href=\"/guides/patch-notes/\"><span>Patch check</span>Compare game updates before enabling an older profile</a>\n            </div>\n        </section>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <p>&copy; <span data-current-year>2026</span> Megabonk.org — Unofficial fan resource. Third-party mods are not endorsed by Megabonk.org or the game developer.</p>\n    </footer>\n    <script src=\"/js/current-year.js\" defer></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}
